    <h1>Mini Biography of Malala Yousafzai</h1>

    <h2>About Malala</h2>

    <p>
        <strong>Malala Yousafzai</strong> is a Pakistani
        education activist who was born on 12 July 1997.
        She is famous for standing up for the right of
        every girl to receive an education.
    </p>

    <h2>Her Early Life</h2>

    <p>
        Malala grew up in Pakistan, where she developed
        a strong passion for learning. From a young age,
        she believed that <em>every child deserves the
        opportunity to go to school.</em>
    </p>

    <h2>Her Achievements</h2>

    <p>
        In 2014, Malala became the youngest person to
        receive the <strong>Nobel Peace Prize</strong>.
        She continues to campaign for girls' education
        around the world.
    </p>

    <h2>Her Famous Quote</h2>

    <blockquote>
        "One child, one teacher, one book, and one pen
        can change the world."
    </blockquote>

    <p>
        This quote reminds us that <u>education is
        powerful</u> and can make a difference in society.
    </p>

    <h2>Why I Admire Her</h2>

    <p>
        I admire Malala because she is brave, determined
        and passionate about education. She inspires
        young people to stand up for what they believe in.
    </p>

